    "significance": "This work represents a watershed moment in neurotechnology: the first sustained, independent use of an intracortical BCI outside a clinical laboratory without expert supervision. Achieving reliable at-home speech decoding and cursor control over extended periods validates the real-world viability of implantable BCIs and removes a critical hurdle toward clinical adoption. This directly demonstrates that BCIs can transition from experimental devices to functional prosthetics for severely paralyzed patients."
